# Copy to .env.local to override. Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_.

# Base URL for the API.
#
# Leave this unset for normal development and for production. The default is the relative path
# `/api`, which is correct in both cases: the Vite dev server proxies /api to the backend on :8080
# (see vite.config.ts), and in production the SPA is served from inside the backend JAR. Both are
# same-origin.
#
# Setting an absolute cross-origin URL here (e.g. http://localhost:8080/api) will break at runtime,
# and not in an obvious way. Two defects in SecurityConfig.corsConfigurationSource() make the
# backend's CORS unusable from a browser:
#
#   1. allowedOrigins("*") is combined with allowCredentials(true) — a combination Spring has
#      rejected since 5.3. It throws during request processing rather than degrading gracefully.
#   2. allowedMethods omits PATCH, so preflight fails for every PATCH endpoint: marking a
#      notification read, marking all read, partial profile update, and the post premium toggle.
#
# Override it only for a non-browser client, or once those two are fixed on the backend.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
